WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.736 --> 00:00:01.600
- [Narrator] Hair trends.

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:03.840
As quickly as they appear, they disappear.

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:05.653
Except for this one.

00:00:05.653 --> 00:00:08.480
Men's powdered wigs, a
trend that strangely lasted

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:11.403
a century and had close
ties not to fashion

00:00:11.403 --> 00:00:12.570
but to an STD.

00:00:17.525 --> 00:00:19.765
Powdered wigs, also known as perukes,

00:00:19.765 --> 00:00:22.197
were all the rage in the 1700s.

00:00:22.197 --> 00:00:25.109
They were the hot item
for aristocratic men.

00:00:25.109 --> 00:00:27.168
But it wasn't a stylistic choice.

00:00:27.168 --> 00:00:28.992
Rather men mostly wore the wigs

00:00:28.992 --> 00:00:30.912
because of syphilis.

00:00:30.912 --> 00:00:33.173
Starting in 1580, syphilis outbreaks

00:00:33.173 --> 00:00:35.307
spread to become one
of the worst epidemics

00:00:35.307 --> 00:00:38.645
to ever hit Europe, on
par with The Black Death.

00:00:38.645 --> 00:00:40.853
There were no antibiotics
to combat the disease, and

00:00:40.853 --> 00:00:43.189
so victims faced blindness, dementia,

00:00:43.189 --> 00:00:46.018
hair loss and even open sores.

00:00:46.018 --> 00:00:47.952
At that time going bald was considered

00:00:47.952 --> 00:00:49.496
quite embarrassing.

00:00:49.496 --> 00:00:52.045
As syphilis spread, the
wig makers got busy.

00:00:52.045 --> 00:00:54.392
They created beautiful
perukes coated with powder

00:00:54.392 --> 00:00:56.248
and even scented with lavender to hide

00:00:56.248 --> 00:00:57.795
any unpleasant smells.

00:00:57.795 --> 00:01:00.173
At this point the wigs were
not yet considered stylish

00:01:00.173 --> 00:01:03.576
but all that changed
in 1655 when Louis XIV

00:01:03.576 --> 00:01:05.283
started going bald.

00:01:05.283 --> 00:01:07.277
Clearly the King of
France couldn't be seen

00:01:07.277 --> 00:01:08.557
without hair.

00:01:08.557 --> 00:01:10.680
So he did what any man of that day would,

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:11.544
he bought a wig.

00:01:11.544 --> 00:01:14.307
Well actually he hired
48 of the best wig makers

00:01:14.307 --> 00:01:15.949
to create him a custom wig.

00:01:15.949 --> 00:01:17.699
Five years later, the King of England did

00:01:17.699 --> 00:01:18.680
the same thing.

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:20.867
Shortly thereafter
aristocrats followed suit

00:01:20.867 --> 00:01:23.867
and thus the term "bigwig" was born.

